\subsubsection{Tap and LongTap in \citev{vtk-js}}

On a phone, where nothing can be right-clicked, the LongTap is the natural
replacement for opening contextual menus, and the Tap complements it. These two
gestures did not exist in vtk-js, so they were added to its
\texttt{RenderWindowInteractor}: a touch or pen pointer that stays within a
configurable \texttt{longTapDistance} for at least a configurable
\texttt{longTapDuration} emits a LongTap event, otherwise a Tap event is
emitted. A deep dive in the gesture detection was performed, the following BPMN
graph summarizes the gesture detection algorithm including Tap and LongTap
(fig:gesture-detection) \cref{pr:Kitware/vtk-js/3596}.

